WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.216
- But who's this?

00:00:01.216 --> 00:00:02.049
- Don't know.

00:00:02.049 --> 00:00:02.998
That's Klaus.

00:00:02.998 --> 00:00:07.580
(upbeat jolly Christmas music)

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:10.023
- Mr. Klaus, you have a gift.

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:15.930
You were meant for
making toys so I figured,

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.330
if you donate your old toys,

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.770
I'll deliver them for free.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:23.590
(relaxing melodic music)

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.840
- Well, I thought it was
like a good Christmas film,

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.070
like, it was like, for me,

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:29.730
it was like Rise of the Guardians,

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.190
but like, in like, a
different sort of way,

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:33.810
it was like around that context.

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:34.830
- Right, oh blimey!

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:35.663
Okay!

00:00:35.663 --> 00:00:37.000
Are you a film critic?

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.806
Yeah!
- You should be a film critic!

00:00:38.806 --> 00:00:39.639
(boy sighs)

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:41.800
Can you tell me a bit about
the film, what happens?

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.703
- So, basically, the end or the beginning?

00:00:45.703 --> 00:00:47.634
No, don't!
- No spoilers!

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:48.467
(boy laughs)

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:49.510
It's not Breaking Bad.

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:52.110
- That's the postman.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:53.260
- Hello!

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:54.525
Jesper, your handsome postman.

00:00:54.525 --> 00:00:56.400
(wood breaking)

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.339
- About Jesper?

00:00:57.339 --> 00:00:58.172
- Yeah!

00:00:58.172 --> 00:00:59.005
- Yeah.

00:00:59.005 --> 00:01:00.200
- Who was sent to...

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.320
I forgot the name of the village.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:04.570
- He was a bit crazy.

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:06.070
- Who did Klaus remind you of?

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.063
- Santa!

00:01:08.063 --> 00:01:09.200
- No, don't tell him anything.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.240
(boy laughs)

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:11.230
- Santa Klaus!

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:13.230
- He reminds me a bit
of Santa Klaus as well.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:14.440
Look, is it the beard?

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.390
- [Klaus] Let's go!

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:17.687
Ho, ho, ho.

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:19.603
- Wait, wait, wait!
(Klaus laughs)

00:01:19.603 --> 00:01:20.436
Time out, really?

00:01:20.436 --> 00:01:21.269
(Klaus laughs)

00:01:21.269 --> 00:01:22.102
That's how you laugh?

00:01:22.102 --> 00:01:23.880
- I thought it was, yeah, really good.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:27.630
- It was really happy but
at the end it was quite sad.

00:01:28.538 --> 00:01:29.371
- What happened?

00:01:29.371 --> 00:01:30.300
- Not a word!

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.133
You just sit there!

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.750
Be all magical and awesome!

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:35.190
- Which bit was your favorite bit?

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:36.799
- When I met Santa.

00:01:36.799 --> 00:01:38.440
- Why does he have a belt?

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.250
- Because otherwise his
trousers would fall down

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:41.130
and we'd see his pants!

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:43.590
We don't wanna see Jesper's pants, do we?

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:44.650
What the...?
- Loser!

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:46.200
- Oh yeah! Well, if I'm a loser,

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.510
then you're, you're a, you're
a, your not, you're too far,

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:50.343
you're gone!

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:52.673
- Have you asked Klaus for
anything for this Christmas?

00:01:53.728 --> 00:01:54.969
- A drone.

00:01:54.969 --> 00:01:55.802
- A drone!

00:01:55.802 --> 00:01:56.970
Can you, can you sort a drone out?

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:58.260
- And me!

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.453
- And you, you want a drone as well?

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:03.370
Can you do two, two drones Klaus?

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:06.310
And what kind of message do
you think it gave everybody?

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:09.314
- It gave that you should
be good for Christmas.

00:02:09.314 --> 00:02:12.204
- If you be kind to one person,

00:02:12.204 --> 00:02:16.630
then the person you were kind to is kind

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:18.260
to someone else and it
just keeps on going.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:22.020
- We need to show people
that a true selfless act

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:22.853
always sparks another.

00:02:22.853 --> 00:02:23.686
(small girl giggles)

00:02:23.686 --> 00:02:26.320
- If you tell one person, be nice to them,

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:28.040
they will be nice to another person.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.920
- Christmas isn't just
about getting presents.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:32.693
There is a deeper meaning to it.

00:02:32.693 --> 00:02:33.526
- No!

00:02:34.448 --> 00:02:36.130
(Jesper screaming)

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.520
- Ha, eat our snow you...

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:39.360
They're not attached.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:40.310
Why aren't they attached?

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:41.490
I thought they were attached.

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:44.670
I would never in a million
years have done what I just did

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.563
if I didn't think these were attached.

